Speaking of bit rot and the evaporation of code, which we're
about to do...

Once upon a time, back in the middle 1980's, before I
realized that each of the levels of Larn was fixed and hand
drawn, just apparently used in some non-fixed order, I
reverse engineered the imagined "code" for several of the
levels to have something that made similar levels from first
principles. Naturally, that code is Gone with the Wind
today, computer media both changes too fast and gets lost
too easily for personal software to last long, but it might
be a fun project for someone else to repeat [and debug
carefully, there are lots of nooks and crannies of ways to
do it incorrectly, I recall as if it were yesterday], then
submit to the Dev Team as possible alternative level
generators for NetHack.  I remember the task being easy
enough to be done just for the fun of doing it, even in C,
and I managed to reproduce the styles of four or five of
the levels, IIRC.

I suppose that counts as a YANI, so I changed the Subject.

